language js

// Replaces the ESLint `no-restricted-syntax` rule that banned
// `MemberExpression[property.name='randomUUID']`.
//
// `crypto.randomUUID` only exists in a SECURE context. PortOS is routinely reached
// over plain HTTP via Tailscale, where it is undefined — so every bare call is a
// crash for the users on that deployment (it took out every toast until
// `lib/uuid.js` landed). The footgun was independently rediscovered at half a dozen
// sites, each inventing a different workaround, so a shared helper alone was not
// enough to stop it: this rule is what actually holds the line.
//
// Biome's `nursery/noJsRestrictedProperties` is NOT a substitute, for the same
// reason `no-restricted-properties` was not: it misses `globalThis.crypto.randomUUID`.
//
// Matching on the CST node kind with a `member` constraint (rather than on code
// snippets) is what makes this exhaustive. It reaches every form ESLint's AST
// selector did, in one pattern per node kind:
//   * `crypto.randomUUID()`            plain member call
//   * `globalThis.crypto.randomUUID()` nested — the case that defeats property bans
//   * `window.crypto.randomUUID()` / `self.crypto.randomUUID()`
//   * `crypto?.randomUUID?.()`         optional chaining (`?.` is the same CST kind)
//   * `typeof crypto.randomUUID`       bare reference, not just calls
//   * `crypto.randomUUID = fn`         assignment target (JsStaticMemberAssignment)
// Like the ESLint selector, it deliberately does NOT match the computed form
// `crypto['randomUUID']` (no `property.name`) or destructuring.
//
// Exemptions (`src/lib/uuid.js`, `src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}`) are applied in biome.jsonc
// via negated globs on the override that loads this plugin.
or {
  JsStaticMemberExpression(member = $member),
  JsStaticMemberAssignment(member = $member)
} as $node where {
  $member <: `randomUUID`,
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $node,
    message = "crypto.randomUUID is undefined on insecure origins (PortOS over plain HTTP via Tailscale). Import { uuidv4 } from lib/uuid.js instead.",
    severity = "error"
  )
}
